{"id":"n-20261012-n0y99c","category":"gaming","display_title":"Games Like Cyberpunk 2077","display_title_he":"משחקים בסגנון סייברפאנק 2077","short_summary":"A guide highlights eight video games for players looking for dystopian themes, corporate corruption, and complex choices similar to Cyberpunk 2077.","english_level":"C1","words":464,"reading_time":3,"image":null,"sources":[{"name":"Polygon","domain":"polygon.com","url":"https://www.polygon.com/best-games-like-cyberpunk-2077","title":"8 Best Cyberpunk 2077 Replacement Games","published_at":"2026-10-12T01:29:05.000Z"}],"published_at":"2026-10-12T01:29:05.000Z","first_published_in_app_at":"2026-10-12T07:28:47.976Z","quality_score":9,"interest_score":9,"verification_status":"verified","content_status":"published","paragraphs":["Finishing a sprawling futuristic role-playing game often leaves players yearning for a similar atmosphere, rich in neon aesthetics, corporate corruption, and deep existential questions. For those who recently completed Cyberpunk 2077 and found themselves longing for more dystopian storytelling, industry guides have highlighted eight alternative titles that capture various elements of that memorable experience, according to recent gaming overviews.","Among the recommendations is Deus Ex: Mankind Divided, a title set in 2029 that dives deep into corporate conspiracies, the ethics of human augmentation, and physical identity struggles. Players guide Adam Jensen through locations like Prague while navigating threats from rogue arms dealers, murderous mercenaries in creepy gold masks, and mysterious organizations like the Illuminati. Similarly, Watch Dogs: Legion offers a deep dive into an authoritarian surveillance state in London, where a mysterious group named Zero Day frames the resistance hacker syndicate DedSec for lethal bombings.","Instead of following a single predefined protagonist, players can recruit almost any ordinary citizen on the street to help DedSec clear its name and free their city. For players interested in exploring the broader catalog of Cyberpunk 2077 developer CD Projekt Red, The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt provides a dark fantasy alternative. While it trades futuristic neon for a medieval landscape populated by monsters and a mutant hunter named Geralt searching for his daughter Ciri, both games share a dark tone where ethical decisions remain profoundly complicated.","Another title focusing on corporate collapse is The Ascent, an isometric action game set on a towering planet called Veles, where a mega-corporation's sudden bankruptcy plunges a massive residential tower into sudden anarchy from the grimiest level known as the deepStink. Other games approach the dystopian genre from entirely different mechanical angles. Cloudpunk places players in the role of an illicit delivery worker named Rania navigating a vertical sci-fi metropolis without any combat, focusing purely on narrative atmosphere and the rigid rules of a delivery service.","Ghostwire: Tokyo combines futuristic urban exploration with supernatural elements, tasking a possessed protagonist named Akito and a spectral detective named KK with stopping an occultist after a deadly fog transforms citizens into loose spirits and piles of clothes. Meanwhile, Observer offers a psychological horror experience where a neural detective named Daniel Lazarski must hack into the minds of apartment residents in a lockdown building to solve a murder, locate his estranged son, and investigate a digital plague known as the nanophage.","Finally, VA-11 HALL-A scales down the apocalyptic setting into an intimate bartending simulation. Set in Glitch City where nanomachines control everyday life, players serve drinks as a cynical bartender named Jill Stingray to various patrons, listening to their personal tragedies, loneliness, and financial struggles. Together, these eight titles demonstrate that while Night City is unique, the broader landscape of digital dystopias offers plenty of compelling reasons to keep playing."],"facts":[{"fact":"Polygon published a guide featuring eight games to play after finishing Cyberpunk 2077, highlighting titles that share similar dystopian, corporate, or sci-fi themes.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Deus Ex: Mankind Divided features corporate conspiracies, augmentation ethics, and a protagonist dealing with identity struggles in a futuristic setting.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Watch Dogs: Legion places players in an authoritarian London where the hacker group DedSec can recruit everyday citizens.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Witcher 3: Wild Hunt, created by Cyberpunk 2077 developer CD Projekt Red, offers a dark fantasy story with complex moral choices and a recent remaster.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"The Ascent is a top-down isometric game set in a tower-city run by a mega-corporation that suddenly goes bankrupt, leading to corporate anarchy.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Cloudpunk is a delivery game where players navigate a vertical sci-fi city following strict rules without any combat.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Ghostwire: Tokyo combines a broken futuristic city with supernatural elements, urban legends, and an occultist who covers the city in deadly fog.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"Observer is a psychological horror game where a neural detective named Daniel Lazarski hacks into the minds of residents in a lockdown apartment building.","sources":[1]},{"fact":"VA-11 HALL-A is an intimate game where players work as a bartender in Glitch City, listening to the struggles and stories of various patrons.","sources":[1]}],"glossary":[{"text":"Finishing","lemma":"finish","pos":"verb","he":"לסיים","name":false},{"text":"sprawling","lemma":"sprawling","pos":"adjective","he":"מתפשט, רחב ידיים","name":false},{"text":"futuristic","lemma":"futuristic","pos":"adjective","he":"עתידני","name":false},{"text":"role-playing game","lemma":"role-playing game","pos":"noun","he":"משחק תפקידים","name":false},{"text":"leaves","lemma":"leave","pos":"verb","he":"משאיר","n